-- The default summary is now a few short paragraphs rather than one. Monitors still on the one-paragraph default move to it.
.bail on
UPDATE monitor SET summary_prompt = 'Write it like a short news item, not a report: a few short paragraphs of one to three sentences each, with a blank line between them. No bullet points, headings or labelled sections, even as plain text: don''t write "Topic: detail" one per line or sentence (for example "Infrastructure: council approved X. Housing: council discussed Y."), which is a list dressed up as prose. Write it the way you''d describe the meeting to someone out loud, with one topic flowing into the next. Focus on the most significant decisions and discussions.'
  WHERE summary_prompt = 'Write 2 to 4 sentences as one flowing paragraph, like a short news item, not a report. No bullet points, headings or labelled sections, even as plain text: don''t write "Topic: detail" one per line or sentence (for example "Infrastructure: council approved X. Housing: council discussed Y."), which is a list dressed up as prose. Write it the way you''d describe the meeting to someone out loud, with one topic flowing into the next. Focus on the most significant decisions and discussions.';
